# broiler-unicode unicode data pin 1
#
# The Unicode Character Database files Broiler.Unicode's algorithm tables are generated from, the
# auxiliary break data and its tests, the two emoji sequence files, the Unicode licence text, and
# ECMA-262's three property tables. The generator (src/Unicode.Generation) reads these files and
# nothing else, and refuses any whose bytes or version header do not match what is recorded here.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. This file and the archive beside it are a copy of Broiler.VM's
# src/tests/unicode/pins/unicode.pin and its archive, taken on 2026-10-16 at milestone SJL-7 (work
# package SJL-7.2) of the shared JavaScript libraries programme, under decision SJL-D-6 (c) and the
# owner condition this repository adopted on that date (docs/roadmap.md): "It starts as a copy of
# Broiler.VM's src/tests/unicode/pins/unicode.pin: the same files, by the same hashes." Every file was
# copied byte for byte from Broiler.VM at 7b44dc7, and every line below names the same file by the
# same length and SHA-256 as Broiler.VM's pin; Broiler.VM's rule I4 and this repository's bundle
# sjl-7-001 (decision-rule.md, part B) hold the two pins equal. Broiler.VM's pin records how each file
# was retrieved from unicode.org and tc39/ecma262, twice and byte-identical, between 2026-09-22 and
# 2026-10-04; nothing here was retrieved again.
#
# ONE DIFFERENCE OF FORM. A `spec-table` line names its file by a path relative to this repository's
# root, so the three ECMAScript tables, archived in Broiler.VM beside its specification edition, sit
# here under data/unicode/pins/ecma262/. Their bytes, lengths and hashes are Broiler.VM's.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. `file <path relative to this directory> <bytes> <sha256>` for a UCD file, an
# emoji file or the licence text; `spec-table <path relative to the repository root> <bytes> <sha256>`
# for an ECMAScript property table. UnicodeData.txt carries no header line and is held by its hash
# alone; every other UCD file's first line names its version, and the emoji files state theirs in a
# `# Version:` line. NormalizationTest.txt and the three auxiliary *BreakTest.txt files are test-only
# input: no table is generated from them.

data unicode-character-database
